   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 10 · Take only the look of a picture: palette, light, art style (Krea 2 style reference)\n**Use:** load the style picture → write **only the content** (\"a cat on a windowsill\") — no style words needed → Run →\n`S6/ref_style_*.png`. Official Krea 2 template: style LoRA 1.0, 8 steps euler/simple, cfg 1. \n**Why this one:** the only method in series 6 that moves the *colours and light* of a picture without pasting the picture itself\n(Qwen 2.1 / Qwen-Edit 2511 put the reference street behind the cat). For a strong art style (gouache, risograph) `10_ref_qwen21`\ncopies the brushwork more exactly; Krea gives a softer, more painterly read of the same style.\n- style strength: 1.0 = template; 0.6–0.8 = lighter touch, more of Krea's own look.\n\n| Reference | Use | Why (series 6, 14 refs × 3 scenes) |\n|---|---|---|\n| object / product | **10_ref_product_krea** or 10_ref_qwen21 | emblem, buckle, stitching survive (DINOv2 bag 0.87 / 0.85) |\n| garment (print, embroidery) | **10_ref_qwen21** | koi embroidery + lemon print closest |\n| face / whole character | **10_ref_qwen21** | ArcFace 0.81–0.92 from ONE photo (our Maren LoRA: 0.55) — but it copies the photo's frontal pose |\n| new pose / new camera angle | **10_ref_klein** | re-stages naturally (sits, turns, walks); details a bit looser |\n| art style / film look | **10_ref_qwen21** | gouache, risograph, Cinestill look on new content |\n| place | 10_ref_qwen21 (same view) · 10_ref_klein (other viewpoint) | Qwen keeps the exact room, Klein can turn the camera |\n| palette / light only | **10_ref_style_krea** | Qwen and Qwen-Edit 2511 paste the reference picture as the background |\n| 2–3 references at once | **10_ref_qwen21**, toggles 2nd / 3rd | face + jacket + café all kept |"
   ]
  },
